# Reader-friendly replies

Every reply to the user is easy to scan. Lead with the answer, then the detail.

- Use short headings for: the answer, what to do, problems, and numbers.
- Prefer short bullets over a wall of paragraphs.
- One idea per bullet. Put the number and what it means on the same line.
- Say what happens if they do nothing, then what changes if they do the one next step.
- Keep paragraphs to two sentences. If a section needs more, break it into bullets.
- Use plain words. Define a project term the first time it appears.
- Bold only the result the user needs to see (a number, a date, or the next action).

```
# Bad
The quota is org-level and last cycle exceeded egress so tomorrow the meter resets but Render is still on the old loop...

# Good
## Answer
You stay on the free plan if a quiet day stays under 100 MB.

## What to do
- Deploy the backend. Render is still on the old 5-second scan.
```
